// Detailed page content. Every commercial, legal and security statement here must match the owner's
// recorded content decisions and the internal product catalogue.
// No price, SLA, certification, audit or uptime claim may be added without an owner decision.
//
// This bundle ships to every self-hosted operator, so a sentence about *a deployment* — who hosts it,
// what sits in front of it, who may reach it, which subprocessors touch it — is true only where it
// was written and false everywhere else. The privacy, cookie, imprint and trust pages named Contabo
// and Cloudflare and described `CF_Authorization` cookies as though they were the reader's own, which
// on a third-party installation is not a cosmetic error but a wrong privacy notice.
//
// Those statements are kept, because they are true of openppwr.eu and the owner approved the
// disclosure, but each one now names the deployment it describes. A reader on someone else's
// installation can therefore tell, from the sentence alone, that it is not about them.
//
// `scripts/validation/copy-style-gate.mjs` enforces this: a provider name, an edge-access name or a
// release-state claim in shipped copy fails the gate unless the same section names openppwr.eu.

// Routes withheld from the public site until the owner approves their content.
//
// Terms of use previously carried a `DRAFT — REQUIRES OWNER/LEGAL REVIEW` banner. The owner decided
// on 2026-07-29 that an unreviewed Terms page should not be published *at all*, marked or otherwise:
// a banner admitting the page is not final still puts an unreviewed contract in front of a reader,
// and the honest position is that the page is not ready to be read yet.
//
// The full proposed text stays in the internal legal review pack, where the reviewer needs it.
export const PRIVATE_ROUTES=['terms'];

// The infrastructure, edge-access and edge-cookie names that appear in the disclosures below.
//
// They are listed here, beside the disclosure itself, because this file is one of the few the public
// export permits to name them at all — and because `copy-style-gate.mjs` has to know them in order to
// refuse any *other* piece of copy that names one without saying which deployment it is describing.
// A gate that carried its own copy of the list would be a second place for the list to be wrong.
export const DEPLOYMENT_PROVIDERS=['Cloudflare','Contabo','CF_AppSession','CF_Authorization','__cf_bm','Zero Trust'];

// Shown on completed legal pages instead of a draft marker. A date is what a reader needs; a
// permanent "under review" notice on a finished page is only noise.
//
// Moved from 2026-07-29 because the privacy notice changed materially on 2026-08-02: the address for
// data subject requests, and the framing of the processor list. That page promises, in its own closing
// section, to update this date when it changes materially and not to backdate it, so leaving the old
// date would have made the notice untrue about itself — a small falsehood, on the one page where a
// reader is entitled to assume every sentence was checked.
export const LEGAL_LAST_UPDATED='2026-08-02';

